Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.37,0:00:05.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}A bicycle dynamo turns motion into\Nelectricity, using a built-in magnet.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.82,0:00:09.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}The Earth has to make its\Nown. The trick: a loop.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.61,0:00:14.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Hold a microphone near its own\Nspeaker, and turn up the {\c&H7AAF1B&}gain{\c&HF7F4F2&}.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.72,0:00:17.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Below a certain point, a whisper fades.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.04,0:00:20.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Past it, the loop feeds itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.55,0:00:27.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Now spin a copper disc wired\Nto a coil around its axle.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.40,0:00:30.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Current makes {\c&H3468EB&}field{\c&HF7F4F2&},\Nand field makes current.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.66,0:00:34.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Spin it faster and faster.\NDoes the field grow bit by bit,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.77,0:00:37.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}or not at all until some speed?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.03,0:00:43.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Not at all, until a threshold.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.87,0:00:46.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Past it, each turn multiplies a tiny
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.71,0:00:50.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}{\c&H3468EB&}seed field{\c&HF7F4F2&} by the same factor:\Nexponential growth.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.51,0:00:54.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Just past the threshold, growth is slow.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.85,0:00:58.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Then the field brakes the\Ndisc, and growth stops.
